# Licensing

architecture-pattern is permissively licensed to encourage the widest possible
adoption: private, public, academic and commercial. Attribution is the primary
expectation.

## Two licences, by file type

| Asset | Licence | SPDX identifier |
|-------|---------|-----------------|
| Documentation, skill instructions, templates, examples and diagrams (Markdown, YAML, JSON models, draw.io, images) | Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International | `CC-BY-4.0` |
| Executable code and its declarations (Python under `scripts/`, shell scripts, `inputs.toml`, plugin manifests, CI workflows) | Apache License, Version 2.0 | `Apache-2.0` |

Per-file licensing is declared with SPDX identifiers and the `REUSE.toml`
manifest at the repository root, following the
[REUSE Specification 3.3](https://reuse.software/spec-3.3/). The full licence
texts are in `LICENSES/`. The skill directory, `skills/pattern/`, carries its own
copy of this file, the licence texts and the `NOTICE`, so a copy of that
directory on its own is complete.

## Origin

This work is derived from the `pattern` skill of AI-Assisted Architecture by
Dermot O'Brien, https://github.com/dermot-obrien/ai-assisted-architecture,
which is licensed on the same terms. `NOTICE` records the source repository,
path and commit it was taken from. Keep `NOTICE` with any copy or derivative,
as Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires.

## What you may do

- Use it in any context, including commercial work.
- Apply it on paid client engagements.
- Embed it in commercial products and internal tools.
- Modify, fork and redistribute it.
- Translate it.

## What we ask in return

- Attribute the original. Both CC BY 4.0 and Apache-2.0 require attribution
  to the original author. Keep author, copyright and `NOTICE` contents intact,
  and link back to https://github.com/dermot-obrien/architecture-pattern when
  reasonable.
- Indicate changes. If you modify the work, mark what you changed.

